
Pixel: position, color; physical characteristics of an emissive light source
Frame: array of pixels, normalized positions: {[0, 1), [0, 1)}; physical size of the pixel array
Layout: arrangement of pixels (rectangular, radial); does not take part in animation calculations, only the final rendering of the frame
Panel: layout, pixel radius, physical dimensions and spacing of pixel array; does not take part in animation calculations, only the final rendering of the frame
Pattern: array of color values, positions: {[0, 1), [0, 1)}; maps to pixel array based on view and animation parameters
    pattern files provide default values for layout, physical dimensions (size and counts), view parameters, animation parameters; should not be part of pattern class
Viewport: position (current view position), size
Animation: velocity, transition, dissolve duration, dissolve time
Scene: frame, panel, viewport, animation, 2 patterns to account for dissolves
    updates frame: applies velocity and viewport to pattern(s), interpolates if within dissolve
Application:
    scene.update()
    scene.draw()

layout, velocity vector changes are immediate
durations are in s
distances are in mm
velocity is in mm / s
viewport (and velocity vector) changes are immediate, but only apply to target pattern in a dissolve
starting view positions need not be origin, but if not, and only when starting a dissolve, should probably be copied from original view

velocity is the virtual movement of the frame/view over the pattern
viewport is the portion of the pattern that is visible
viewport maps exactly to the frame


Pixel: size, position, color
Frame: 2D array of pixels
Pattern: frame, viewport, layout, animation
Shot: frame, pattern, viewport position
Controller: frame&, shots

Pixel: same
PixelArray: 2D array of pixels
Panel: size, arrangement of pixels

